<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="vendor/autoload.php"
         cacheDirectory=".phpunit.cache"
         colors="true"
         failOnDeprecation="true"
         failOnNotice="true"
         failOnWarning="true">
    <php>
        <env name="KERNEL_CLASS" value="Uhifadhi\Shell\Tests\Integration\TestKernel"/>
        <!--
            THERE IS NO DATABASE ENV HERE, AND THERE WILL NOT BE ONE. The shell
            draws; it does not remember. A shell that needed a connection to
            render a page would have acquired a domain, and Unit/BoundaryTest
            fails the build the moment doctrine appears in its requirements.
        -->
    </php>
    <testsuites>
        <!--
            ONE SUITE, GREEN, AND IT STAYS GREEN. The bundle boots, its
            container compiles, its config tree holds, its Twig namespace
            resolves, the boundaries hold — and the socket contract renders:
            twenty-three blocks on three frames, twenty-three theme tokens, two
            seams, the tab strip and the catalogue picture.

            The contract was written first, as a separate suite that failed on
            purpose, and it stayed separate exactly as long as it was red so
            that "red by design" and "broken" could never be confused. The
            extraction landed; there is nothing left to keep apart.
        -->
        <testsuite name="shell">
            <directory>tests/Unit</directory>
            <directory>tests/Integration</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <source restrictNotices="true" restrictWarnings="true">
        <include>
            <directory>src</directory>
        </include>
    </source>
</phpunit>
